        definition("direction_import", "Import a local video/audio/image file. References originals without modifying them; HDR video (an iPhone's HLG, PQ) comes in as an SDR Rec.709 copy Direction makes in the film's Footage folder, and the asset's sdrCopyOf names the original; a file with open keyframes (FFmpeg's x265), whose frames just before a keyframe the player can't start on, comes in as a copy rewritten without re-encoding, named by seekableCopyOf. Set append to place it at the end of a sequence. The first picture into a film with nothing cut sets the cuts' size and frame rate (frameRate overrides the rate). library instead of path brings in a sound or image from the director's library by name (direction_library): the film gets its own copy, which isn't footage; asked again, it's the copy already in.", ["path": string, "library": string, "append": bool, "sequenceID": string, "frameRate": number, "baseEditRevision": integer, "idempotencyKey": string], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_edit", "The only way to change a cut: a batch of named edit functions that Direction carries out exactly, as one new revision or not at all. With measure: true, a batch that changes the sound (gain, fade, duck, audio, placeMusic, parts, loudness, syncSound) answers with mix: the whole mix as it now measures (integratedLUFS, truePeakDBTP, the target's verdict, the loudest stretches, anything over the ceiling), so there's no separate call to measure after it. Read direction_timeline first for clip ids and the editRevision. Send {baseEditRevision, idempotencyKey, summary, notes:[note numbers it answers], validateOnly?, operations:[{op, …}]}; an operation may name its own note. A batch with no note is allowed only with latitude free (labeled Unasked) or outside a notes turnover. Times are cut seconds unless an argument says source; frames count frames at the cut's rate; results snap to whole frames. An edit point is \"<left clip>|<right clip>\". Story (V1; every layer stays in sync): insert(assetID,sourceRange,at,track?), overwrite(same), removeRange(range,ripple?), remove(clipID,ripple?), move(clipID,to:{at|before|after}), split(clipID,at,snap?), trim(clipID,edge:head|tail,frames ±,ripple?,snap?), roll(editPoint,frames,snap?) (snap: blink|action|pause, the nearest within 8 frames), slip(clipID,frames), slide(clipID,frames), splitEdit(editPoint,lead:sound|picture,frames), replaceTake(clipID,withAssetID,alignOn:words|head|tail), removeWords(wordIDs), tightenPauses(range,longerThan,to), speed(clipID,rate,ripple?), freeze(clipID,at,seconds). Picture: reframe(clipID,scale,x?,y?,follow?:face|subject,keepIn?:thirds|center), balance(clipID,exposure?,contrast?,saturation?,temperature?,tint?), matchBalance(clipID,toClipID), cameraLUT(assetID,lut:auto|none|file), addEffect(target:clip|track,effect,params,keys?) returns effectID, setEffect(effectID,params?,keys?), removeEffect(effectID), transition(editPoint,type:dissolve|dipToBlack|dipToWhite|push|slide|whip|zoom|wipe|iris|shader,frames,params?), removeTransition(editPoint). Layers: cutaway(assetID,sourceRange,at|cover), pin(clipID,corners?,follow?:screen) puts a V2+ clip into a screen in the shot under it, zoomThrough(editPoint,seconds?,corners?) pushes into a screen in the left shot and through to the right one, placeGraphic(graphic,at,seconds?,aboveLook?), placeMade(madeID,at,track,sourceRange?). Sound: gain(target,dB,keys?), fade(clipID,in?,out? frames), duck(track,under,dB,attack?,release?), placeMusic(madeID|assetID,at,endOn,from?,parts?,track?), parts(clipID,heard:{part:[{start,end}]},frames?), audio(assetID|clipID,audioTrackID,audio: only what changes). Finishing, done by Direction exactly: loudness(lufs?,truePeak?) measures the mix and sets the whole mix's gain to the target from Settings, as far as the \u{2212}1 dBTP ceiling allows; captions(range?,wordsAtATime?) lays captions from the cut's words as graphics, in place of the ones it laid before; credits(at?,seconds?) rolls the director's credits on black after the last shot. A library song's parts (stems, full mix) play the same moment of it wherever they meet: move, slip, fade and duck take them together. Film: format, duplicateSequence. Effects (direction_edit_catalog has every parameter's range and default): transform, pin, blend, mask, blur, sharpen, stabilize, filter.<kind>, shader (params.file Effects/<name>.metal, checked on 3 frames at 1080p). Transitions other than dissolve and the dips are Metal too: Direction's own by type, or yours with type shader and params.file Transitions/<name>.metal. validateOnly returns the predicted result without committing. The result lists, per operation, its summary, notes, delta and changed ranges in the new and old cut with their scenes. Errors are {index, code, message}: scene_locked, picture_locked, stale_revision, overlap, unknown_op, bad_argument, missing_media, no_words, look_is_yours, words_are_yours, shader_invalid, shader_too_slow, no_screen.", ["validateOnly": bool], readOnly: false),
