        definition("direction_transcribe", "Start on-device transcription of a chosen embedded audio track with the engine the director chose in Settings › Engines: apple (SpeechAnalyzer, fast) or whisper (mlx-whisper, slower, sometimes better words). Either way Direction holds each word\u{2019}s start and end to the take\u{2019}s own sound afterwards, so transcribing again doesn\u{2019}t make the times better. engine overrides it; model names a Whisper model. First use may download the model. Returns a job; poll direction_job.", ["assetID": string, "trackID": integer, "language": string, "engine": string, "model": string], required: ["assetID"], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_measure_audio", "Measure sound. Without assetID: the cut's mix as it plays and delivers (every track, gain, fade, duck and audio setting), measured to ITU-R BS.1770-4 / EBU R128: integratedLUFS (K-weighted, 400 ms blocks, gated at −70 LUFS and 10 LU under; null when there's nothing to measure), samplePeakDBFS and truePeakDBTP (4× oversampled), over the whole cut or start–end in cut seconds, at revision (latest by default). ranges measures several stretches in one answer ([{start, end}], up to 20), each with its integratedLUFS and peaks: one call, not one per stretch. profile shows how it moves, in one answer: short-term loudness (3 s) every second, the loudest stretches, the peaks and any over the ceiling, in cut seconds; no need to measure window by window. For the whole cut, target says whether it's ready to deliver against Settings' target and the \u{2212}1 dBTP ceiling; the loudness edit function brings it there. With assetID: one take's track as recorded, its sample peak, RMS and a bounded waveform; those are not LUFS or true peak. levels gives the level every frame over a stretch, each window's peak and RMS in dBFS, in one answer (up to 6,000 windows; every sets the window in seconds, one frame by default): the cut's mix in cut seconds, or with assetID the take's own track in its seconds, so nothing has to be laid out alone to hear it. Use it to find where speech really starts and stops, which the words' times only approximate.", ["assetID": string, "trackID": integer, "revision": integer, "sequenceID": string, "start": number, "end": number, "ranges": list(.object(["type": .string("object"), "properties": .object(["start": number, "end": number])])),
                                                                                                                                       "levels": noted(record(["start": number, "end": number, "every": number], required: ["start", "end"]), "A stretch to measure every frame: {start, end, every?} in seconds (the cut's, or the take's with assetID).")]),
        definition("direction_frame", "Render an actual edited frame using the Metal compositor. Returns inline PNG and exact revision/time context. With assetID, time is source seconds and the frame is that take's own, not the cut's. times renders up to 8 frames of the cut in one answer, each its own image (smaller, 640 by default): look at several moments in one call, not one call each.", ["time": number, "times": list(number), "revision": integer, "sequenceID": string, "maxDimension": integer, "assetID": string]),
        definition("direction_export", "Start native video export of a pinned edit. Presets h264/hevc (MP4), prores (MOV), or timeline: a new folder at path with the cut as FCPXML for Final Cut Pro and DaVinci Resolve, ProRes renders of what only Direction draws, the sound as WAV stems and the look as LUTs. width and height render at another size of the same shape, such as the footage's 3840 × 2160 for a 1920 × 1080 cut. Never overwrites existing files. Returns a durable job record; poll direction_job.", ["path": string, "preset": string, "revision": integer, "sequenceID": string, "width": integer, "height": integer], required: ["path"], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_preview", "Render a short edited video/audio sample to a local artifact. Range in sequence seconds, maximum 30 seconds. Returns a job.", ["start": number, "end": number, "revision": integer, "sequenceID": string], required: ["start", "end"], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_job", "Read job progress/result. Jobs continue while their starting app or MCP process is running. wait stays until the job is over, up to that many seconds (240 at most), and answers with it then: one call instead of asking again and again.", ["jobID": string, "wait": noted(number, "Seconds to wait for it to finish, up to 240.")], required: ["jobID"]),
        definition("direction_jobs", "List durable job records."),
        definition("direction_cancel_job", "Cancel a job owned by this process. Other processes can inspect it but must cancel it in its owner.", ["jobID": string], required: ["jobID"], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_events", "Read ordered project/feedback/job events after a cursor.", ["since": integer]),
    ]

    static func strings(_ values: [String]) -> JSONValue { .object(["type": .string("string"), "enum": .array(values.map(JSONValue.string))]) }
    /// The director–editor protocol. Notes reach the editor only when the director turns them over.
    private static let directingDefinitions: [ToolDefinition] = [
        definition("direction_brief", "Read the director's brief (logline, how it should feel, length, audience, the shape it's cut in (16:9, 9:16, 1:1 or 4:5; none is the footage's own), must-keeps, references, things to avoid, and the style it's cut in) plus the default latitude and lock state. Read it before every assembly or cut; must-keeps are never cut. With a style, read it with direction_style."),
        definition("direction_dailies", "Read the logged footage: scenes, setups, takes with the director's circles, your suggestions and guesses, plus every asset's name and duration. Circles are the director's choices; use circled takes first. syncGroups lists takes that recorded the same moment, matched by sound: soundAssetID is the take whose sound the cut uses (on V1, or under another angle with syncSound), and each take's offset puts it on that take's clock (sound time = take time + offset). A circle on any take in a group asks for that moment."),
        definition("direction_log_dailies", "Log footage as the editor. scenes: [{id?, number, title, setups?:[{code, description}]}]. takes: [{assetID, sceneNumber? or sceneID?, setupCode?, code?, caption?, suggestion? (why you'd pick it), guessSceneNumber? (for takes you can't place), flags?, unusable?}]. You can suggest but never circle. Locked scenes keep their takes.", ["scenes": list(sceneInput), "takes": list(takeInput)], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_turnovers", "Read turnovers: the notes the director handed you, with number, kind (Feeling > Story > Pace > Picture > Sound wins conflicts), anchor, script action, author, replies, latitude (exact, faithful, free), whether to wait for an OK on your read-back, the director's corrections to read-back lines, flipped conflicts and answered questions. libraryNamed says what each '@Name' from the library is; footageNamed says which take, setup or scene each '@2A Take 3', '@2A' or '@Scene 2' is (assetID, what's in it, circled, where it is in the cut). kind 'assembly' asks for a first cut from circled takes.", ["includeClosed": bool]),
        definition("direction_turnover_update", "Report on a turnover. Post readBack:[{noteID, plan (concrete: seconds, dB, which shot), delta?, twoWays?, conflictWithNoteID?, following? (noteID you follow), range? ({start, end} in the cut's seconds), detail?, cantYet?}] before cutting; if waitForOK is true, wait until direction_turnovers shows readBackApproved. Then set state cutting and progress {noteID: queued|working|done|cant|stopped}. Use state blocked or failed with a calm message saying what happened, what's safe and what's next.", ["turnoverID": string, "state": strings(["cutting", "blocked", "failed"]), "readBack": list(readBackLine), "progress": map(strings(["queued", "working", "done", "cant", "stopped"])), "phase": string, "percent": number, "message": string], required: ["turnoverID"], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_ask", "Ask the director to decide, or report a note you can't do as written. kind question needs 2–4 concrete choices [{id?, label, detail?, assetID?, recommended?}]; kind cant explains why (for example a locked scene) and offers up to 4 ways forward. Only the named notes wait; keep cutting the rest. kind spend asks to go over the turnover's spend limit after direction_make said spend_over_limit: spend {estimate, choiceID (the choice that agrees), kind?, version?}; Direction adds what this turnover has spent and the limit. Answers appear in direction_questions.", ["turnoverID": string, "kind": strings(["question", "cant", "spend"]), "noteIDs": list(string), "text": string, "detail": string, "choices": list(choiceInput), "allowsText": bool, "spend": spendQuestionSchema], required: ["kind", "noteIDs", "text", "choices"], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_questions", "Read your questions and can't-do reports with the director's answers."),
        definition("direction_turnover_complete", "Deliver the new cut for a turnover. It's named automatically (Assembly, Cut 2, Cut 3…). answers: [{noteID, summary (first person, concrete), delta? (e.g. −4.2 s, crop, −6 dB), start?, end? (seconds in the new cut, for Play changes), options?:[{label:A|B, summary, revision (where you committed that version; looks carry none), delta?}], preferred?, rule?}]. rule: when a note says something the director would want every time (always, never, a habit they corrected), offer it as {text (one sentence in their words, like \"Text never covers my face\"), area (general, pace, picture, layouts, graphics, captions, transitions, sound, music, color, avoid), scope (style when it's about this kind of video, house when it's about the director), replaces? (ids of rules from direction_style it takes the place of)}; the director decides whether to keep it. Not for one-off fixes. The option committed last is the one in the cut; the director can use the other and Direction swaps it in. With latitude free you may add {unasked:true, summary, kind?, start?, end?} for changes no note asked for. Every change must answer a note or be marked unasked.", ["turnoverID": string, "revision": integer, "sequenceID": string, "answers": list(answerInput)], required: ["turnoverID", "answers"], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_finishing", "After picture lock: read or update the finishing checklist. items: [{id: color|sound|captions|titles|licenses|deliver|…, title?, detail? (words: what it is or what you did), state?: todo|working|done|needsYou|blocked, by?, progress? (a number, 0–1)}]. Also returns the director's credits (a role, then its names, a line each; null until written) and the licenses on file in the film (Licenses/). Finishing can change color, sound and the graphics over the picture (captions, titles, credits), never the cut or its timing.", ["items": list(finishingItem)], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_add_outside_note", "Bring in a note from someone else (producer, client) for the director's Outside inbox. The note stays invisible to you until the director accepts it.", ["name": string, "role": string, "text": string, "time": number, "start": number, "end": number, "sceneID": string, "revision": integer, "cutID": string], required: ["name", "text"], readOnly: false),
        definition("direction_editor_status", "Tell the director's app what you're doing right now, in a few words (shown in the editor pill and popover).", ["phase": string, "detail": string, "progress": number, "agent": string], required: ["phase"], readOnly: false),
    ]
}
